    "notes": "Orca Whirlpool — a concentrated-liquidity AMM (CLMM). Holds the USDG/USDC liquidity Meteora DLMM does not: pool 9RqDTfwCx2SgxsvKpspQHc38HUo3B6hRd3oR9JR966Ps (tick_spacing 1, fee_rate 100 = 0.01%) carried ~$25.68M TVL against DLMM's $0.38, so it is the only venue with BOTH real depth and an ingestible on-chain IDL. VERIFIED AGAINST MAINNET: whirlpool@ts=1 and oracle=['oracle', whirlpool] both reproduce exactly. TRAPS, none of them in the IDL. (1) tick_spacing selects the pool among fee tiers and is NOT derivable from the mints — see why.whirlpool. (2) tick_array is seeded with the ASCII decimal index, not LE — see why.tick_array; span is 88 * tick_spacing. (3) There is NO liquidity bitmap. Unlike DLMM's bin_array_bitmap_extension, Whirlpool has no on-chain index of which tick arrays hold liquidity — array existence must be probed directly. (4) TWO tick-array layouts coexist: fixed TickArray (9,988 bytes) and DynamicTickArray (372 bytes). For the USDG/USDC swap the THIRD array is the dynamic one, so a parser that assumes 9,988 breaks on a real swap. (5) The oracle PDA ['oracle', whirlpool] = 4FQqY5C4fjReyc3MkMRqbR7bk9KRzXdCTbAXb5wbycVh DOES NOT EXIST on chain and must still be passed, WRITABLE. Whether it must be initialized depends on the pool's fee tier being adaptive — a live read, never an IDL fact. (6) swap_v2 (2b04ed0b1ac91e62), not swap (f8c69e91e17587c8): v1 cannot handle a Token-2022 mint, and USDG is Token-2022 while USDC is classic SPL, so token_program_a != token_program_b and memo_program is mandatory. (7) Both user ATAs must be seeded with their OWN mint's token program, read from the mint account's owner — using the wrong one yields a valid, empty, never-initialized account. NOT VERIFIED: Orca's own token_badge recipe is untested here (the address AhSVKq5Wy3yM5S46o9hEFKHmh7s77oAEyeJkUSZg1D9A is Meteora DLMM's badge for USDG under ['token_badge', mint], not Orca's); the a-to-b tick-array boundary shift Orca's SDK applies before flooring is untested at an array edge; adaptive-fee-tier behaviour is inferred from the null oracle, not read; and no Gecko-built raw swap_v2 has been simulated — the passing simulation went through Jupiter's CPI."
